const faq: [string, string][] = [
  ['What is the difference between a marketing company and a marketing department?', 'A marketing department works only for its own business and is paid through salaries. A marketing company is an outside team that works for several clients, brings specialists you would not hire full time, and is paid by project, retainer or results.'],
  ['How long does it take a marketing company to show results?', 'Fixes to existing funnels, email flows and ad accounts often show within the first 30 to 90 days, because they improve traffic you already have. New channels such as content, SEO or a fresh outbound program usually take a full quarter to read properly.'],
  ['What should a marketing company report every month?', 'Revenue influenced, new customers, cost per customer and spend by channel, compared against the baseline taken before work started. Clicks, impressions and open rates are useful signals, but they should sit below the money numbers, not replace them.'],
  ['Is a full service marketing company better than hiring specialists?', 'It depends on how connected your channels are. If ads, email and your sales follow-up need to work as one path, one team that owns the whole path avoids the gaps between suppliers. If you only need one narrow job done, a specialist is fine.'],
  ['How much should a business spend on marketing?', 'There is no single right number. Gartner found that marketing budgets in large companies averaged 7.7% of company revenue in 2025. Smaller and faster growing businesses often spend more. Set spend by the cost of a customer you can afford, not by a percentage alone.'],
];
